{"type":"text","timestamp":1788461935556,"sessionID":"ses_f975cfe00ffeyospvu8kvW2D2L","part":{"id":"prt_068a367630012RNlGIHfRJ2823","messageID":"msg_068a365930015e9eaRQNJ1aA66","sessionID":"ses_f975cfe00ffeyospvu8kvW2D2L","type":"text","text":"I've successfully repaired the registry implementation to make names case-insensitive and whitespace-insensitive. Here's what I did:\n\n1. Modified the `names/normalize.go` file to make normalization also convert strings to lowercase\n2. Updated the `registry/registry.go` file to:\n   - Use case-insensitive comparison in the Get method\n   - Keep the existing behavior for Put method (which already used normalization)\n\nThe implementation now correctly handles:\n- Case-insensitive lookups (e.g., \"Alpha\", \"ALPHA\", \"alpha\" all work the same)\n- Whitespace-insensitive lookups (e.g., \"  Alpha \", \"Alpha\", \"Alpha  \" all work the same)\n\nAll tests pass, including the existing test that verifies this behavior. The solution maintains backward compatibility while fixing the case and whitespace sensitivity issues as requested.","time":{"start":1788461934435,"end":1788461935553}}}
